# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your keys.

# Map tiles and address lookup run on free OpenStreetMap services (Leaflet,
# Nominatim) and need no key. Clinic search uses Google Places when a key is
# present and falls back to OpenStreetMap's Overpass API when it isn't, so the
# Find Care page still works with this left blank — just with worse coverage
# and no phone numbers, hours, or ratings.
#
# (Optional) Google Places API key — primary source for the Find Care map.
# 1. Enable the "Places API (New)" in a Google Cloud project
# 2. Create an API key and restrict it to that one API
# 3. IMPORTANT: set a daily request cap under APIs & Services > Quotas, and a
#    spend cap budget under Billing. A plain budget is an ALERT ONLY and will
#    not stop spending.
# Server-side only. Never give this the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: that inlines it
# into the browser bundle where anyone can lift it and burn your quota.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Anthropic API key — powers personalized risk summaries on the results page
# Get yours at: https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Resend API key — sends screener results by email from the contact form
# Get yours at: https://resend.com/api-keys
RESEND_API_KEY=

# (Optional) HRSA Data Warehouse token — enriches results with FQHC designations
# Request at: https://data.hrsa.gov/tools/web-services
HRSA_API_TOKEN=

# (Optional) Behold.so widget ID — powers the Instagram feed on the homepage
# 1. Go to behold.so and create a free account
# 2. Connect your Instagram account (@oralcheckdotorg)
# 3. Create a new feed, copy the Feed ID
# 4. Paste it here — the section will appear automatically
NEXT_PUBLIC_BEHOLD_WIDGET_ID=
